From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: wpactrl chmod client socket
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

Make hostapd control-interface replies deliverable on OpenWrt.

OpenWrt starts hostapd under procd ujail and drops it to the unprivileged user
"network" (uid 101) while libwifi clients run as root. wpa_ctrl_open() binds the
client socket under the root umask, so hostapd cannot write to it. Traced on the
hostapd side the request arrives and the reply is built - only delivery fails:

  recvfrom(40, "STATUS", ...) from /tmp/wpa_ctrl_928-166 = 6
  sendto(40, "state=ENABLED\nphy=phy0.1\nfreq=5180\n"..., 1223, ...,
         "/tmp/wpa_ctrl_928-166") = -1 EACCES (Permission denied)

hostapd logs that nowhere, so from the client it is indistinguishable from an
unresponsive daemon: select() times out and wpa_ctrl_cmd() returns -2 with an
empty buffer. Every command is affected - STATUS, STATUS-DRIVER, GET_CONFIG,
"get beacon".

hostapd_cli_iface_ap_info() opens with a "get beacon" whose failure sets
ap->enabled = false and returns, so every AP - plain BSS and AP-MLD alike - was
reported disabled, with security/capabilities/bssload left empty. map-agent then
dropped the whole AP-MLD and map-controller stored an all-zero apmld row.

hostapd_cli does fchmod(fd, 0660) before bind, which is why the same commands
work from the shell and fail from libwifi.

Verified on hardware (bpi-4g, OpenWrt 25.12-SNAPSHOT, kernel 6.12.87):
  before: apmld = 1 row of zeros | affiliated_ap = 0 | ttlm = 0
  after:  apmld = OpenWrt-MLD enabled=1 num_ap=3 | affiliated_ap = 3 | ttlm = 24

--- a/libwifi/modules/wpactrl/wpactrl.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/wpactrl/wpactrl.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <net/if.h>
 #include <time.h>
@@ -116,6 +117,19 @@
 		return NULL;
 	}
 
+	/* OpenWrt runs hostapd unprivileged - procd ujail drops it to user
+	 * "network" - while libwifi clients run as root. bind() above created the
+	 * client socket under the root umask, so hostapd cannot write to it: it
+	 * receives the request, builds the reply, and sendto() fails with EACCES.
+	 * It reports that nowhere, so the client just times out. libwifi then
+	 * declares the AP disabled - every AP, plain BSS and AP-MLD alike - and
+	 * map-agent drops the whole AP-MLD as a result.
+	 *
+	 * Make the reply path writable for the unprivileged daemon.
+	 */
+	if (chmod(ctrl->local.sun_path, 0666) < 0)
+		libwifi_dbg("%s: chmod on ctrl socket failed\n", __func__);
+
 	ctrl->dest.sun_family = AF_UNIX;
 
 	if (strlen(ctrl_path) > sizeof(ctrl->dest.sun_path)) {
